ExitStrategy [SimTalk] - Pipe
Sets how the flow rate of the Pipe designated by <Path> is going to be distributed to the succeeding fluid
objects.
Syntax
<Path>.ExitStrategy:string
Type
Attribute
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type string.
You can specify "Evenly distributed" or "Percentage".
Example
MyPipe.ExitStrategy := "Evenly distributed"
See also
Exit Strategy - Pipe
ExitStrategy [SimTalk] - Pipe
11-2702 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

ExitStrategyPercentageValues [SimTalk] - Pipe
Sets the proportional distribution of the flow rate of the Pipe designated by <Path> for the Exit Strategy >
Percentage.
Remarks
Specify 0 in the cell of the respective successor to prevent that successor from receiving any material.
If a successor cannot receive any material, because a succeeding Tank is full for example, the Pipe
distributes the portion of that successor of the flow rate according to the percentages to the remaining
successors.
The sum of the percentages does not have to add up to 100%. Instead, the actual sum of the percentages
of all successors, which can receive material, corresponds to a value of 100%. The percentages [40, 60],
[0.4, 0.6], and [2, 3] are equivalent for example.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.ExitStrategyPercentageValues:array
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type array.
Example
MyPipe.ExitStrategy := "Percentage"
MyPipe.ExitStrategyPercentageValues := [20, 50, 30]
See also
Exit Strategy - Pipe > Percentage [Pipe]
ExitStrategyPercentageValues [SimTalk] - Pipe
